    "access": "team",
    "video1": "The video spoke about subjects that were discussed in class, being the priority of entertainment for the sake of development and education, this also extends to being a fan of your work and making entertaining. the growth mindset was also discussed, an in-class representation of this would be the student mindset and how students should stray away from it in order to actually learn. The video also discusses organization and structure of file systems and their contents this is for being a team member as other developers will be using your files and its important to make it as transparent as possible, this also extends to the contents within files and code like making public classes uppercase and private classes lowercase. The video also discusses the importance of documentation for game development and all development in general this is also for developers as its important for them to know what you've done when you've done it and how you did it. Finally it also it talks about IDEs and the importance of them.",
    "video2": "The developer mindset helps motivate both yourself and your fellow team members and allows everyone to build off each other. Use failure in order. In hard work and dedication you can achieve your goal. It is always helpful to receive",
